+# FINAL POST-REMEDIATION DEEP AUDIT
+
+Generated: 2026-09-23T12:20:28.884686+00:00
+Input source: `FINAL-PROJECT-20260923-115040.zip`
+Input SHA-256: `4ccaa671e04668458b66807f12ef6535aacaf609be082539e827e57ea664fe6e`
+
+## Executive summary
+The exact previous-phase ZIP was extracted into a fresh workspace and re-audited from scratch. The pass covered the frontend/API, authentication and tenant boundaries, PostgreSQL/Drizzle migrations, Go agent, Windows/Tauri boundary, Odoo addon, printing pipeline, billing, dependencies, CI/configuration, UI states, tests, dead-code patterns, and cross-component contracts.
+
+Four new defect classes were verified and fixed: terminal Gateway execution-lease retention, local Agent claim-state retention, silent clipboard failure, and hidden billing-usage failure. Seven regression tests were added in this pass. Existing Tauri token-boundary hardening was independently re-verified in the input ZIP and was not modified.
+
+## Randomized and cross-component review
+Two independent seeded randomized rounds selected 42 files each (84 selections, 74 unique files). Sixteen cross-component flows were traced across both sides of their boundaries; all 16 passed the static contract checks.
+
+## Fixes
+### DEEP-01 — terminal Gateway execution leases
+Some terminal failure paths cleared job status but retained claim credentials/live lease metadata. Those paths now clear `claim_token` and `claimed_at`. The EXPIRED reconciliation path remains intentionally bounded for late physical-result reconciliation.
+
+### DEEP-02 — local Agent claim state
+Terminal `UpdateStatus` and `UpdateStatusWithError` now clear both `claim_token` and `claimed_at`. Crash-recovery code still reads the token before the terminal transition.
+
+### DEEP-03 — clipboard failure UX
+`CopyButton` now surfaces a transient failure state instead of silently swallowing clipboard errors.
+
+### DEEP-04 — billing usage failure UX
+The dashboard now renders an explicit degraded-state message when billing usage cannot be loaded.
+
+## Verification
+`python3 -m pytest -q tests` passed with 68 tests. All Go sources are gofmt-clean. JS/MJS syntax, shell syntax, XML/JSON/YAML/TOML parsing, and ZIP integrity passed. Migration parity was independently recalculated as 67 SQL migrations and 67 journal entries with no duplicate numeric IDs and contiguous numbering.
+
+## Runtime limitations
+The available environment is not the project's supported runtime: Node is 22.16.0 while the repository requires Node >=24.15.0; Go is 1.23.2 while `agent/go.mod` requires 1.26; Rust/cargo, Docker, Odoo runtime, Windows Print Spooler, physical printers, and browser automation are unavailable. These are verification limitations, not claims of source correctness or incorrectness.
+
+## Security / platform research
+Current official guidance was checked for Next.js, Node.js, Drizzle Kit, Odoo 19 security/ORM, Stripe webhooks/idempotency, Go race detection, GitHub Actions version setup, and Win32 printing. The current Next.js CSP guidance confirms nonce-based strict CSP but changing the current `unsafe-inline` policy would affect rendering/caching behavior, so this remains an explicit hardening limitation rather than an unverified architectural change.
+
+## Final production-readiness statement
+All defects identified and reproducible within the available verification environment were fixed. Remaining runtime verification limitations are explicitly documented and require execution in supported Node 24+, Go 1.26, Rust/Tauri, Odoo, Docker/PostgreSQL, and Windows/printer environments.
